    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0692" n="592" xml:id="pg592"/>

                <head>No. 378.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Comly to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-12-22"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 22, 1879</date>.
                        (Received January 23, 1880.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that after
                    correspondence between the Hawaiian foreign office and this legation, and no
                    legal impediment being found to exist, the following American schooners have
                    been registered under the Hawaiian flag: C. M. Ward, General Harney, Joseph
                    Woolley.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES M. COMLY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
